I/ Introduction:
----------------

Caution :
- A psion S3a with 512k is the minimum required,
  but it is strongly recomended to use a Psion with at
  least 1Mo or 2Mo to be able to use conveniently all
  the Ppaint possibilities.
  You can disable spare page, undo or Color to gain memory.

Installation :
--------------
- Integrally copy the drawer "PPAINT" and its content
     in LOC::M:\
     or LOC::A:\
     or LOC::B:\
  All files must stay in PPAINT drawer.
- Install the PPAINT.OPA program with the menu
  "Appli/installer/PPAINT.OPA" at the system screen level.
   A new icon should appear.

Install externals libraries:
----------------------------
In the Ppaint package you can find:
* Firepic.zip (Copyright Andrew Baldwin)
* Gpicgif1.zip (copyright Serge Shestopalov)

- Unzip them and read internals docs.
- Make a drawer named 'DYL' in LOC::M:\
                            or LOC::A:\
                            or LOC::B:\

- Copy 'Gpic$PCX.DYL' (from Firepic.zip) in the DYL drawer.
- Copy 'Gpic$GIF.DYL' (from GPICGIF1.zip) in the DYL drawer.

GPIC$GIF is Shareware, so read the doc before using it.

* GPIC$PCX.dyl can import and export PCX picture but only in CGA & EGA
  format. You can load picture with Floyd dithering, or without
  dithering.

* GPIC$GIF.dyl can import and export GIF picture. You can't load
  picture without dithering.

These Libraries needs a lot of memory, so, save your work first in PIC
format and after, export it.Sometimes an 'Out of memory' can appear
with the GIF format.



Future plans :
- Psion S5 version.

Some of the Ppaint fonctions :
- Ppaint is in French and English
- Load, Save & Edit Picture
- Load, Save & Edit Animation
- Firepic compatibility (Load &Save GIF and PCX format
  with Externals libraries...see DOC)
- Use less memory
- unlimited page size
- Page spare,
- undo available on all funcions,
- textures creation module,
- Fill fonction on spare page or texture,
- 2 level zoom,
- brushes transformation,
- Special effects on current page,
- New Brush
- Anim brush
- State window
- AnimPainting
- AutoAnim
- Curve and Bspline
- etc...


II/ Generality:
---------------
- Move cursor using arrows keys, or Psion+arrow keys for
  a faster move. All the moves are ruled by the Special
  menu Preferences.
- Use 'Shift'+arrows keys to move cursor one pixel per one pixel
- Use Ctrl+Psion+arrows keys to reach the sides of the image.
- The diamond key allows you to change colors or stencils
  (Black, Black&Gray, Gray).
- 'Psion+Help' to move or remove the state window.
- 'TAB' Toggle between pen and brush (if this one exists).
- Functions between brackets are not available yet.
- 'Help' to see help on-line
- If you made an Animation: 
   'Maj' + 'Psion' + '->' GO to the next Frame.
   'Maj' + 'Psion' + '<-' GO to the previous Frame.

With esternals libraries, Ppaint can import & export
GIF & PCX format.



III/ Picture Menu:
------------------
*"Load", loads a picture. If it is different than the Psion's screen
  you can:
   - Select the picture's portion to edit by moving the picture
     using the arrow keys then pressing the spacebar to validate.
   - Modify the size of your page so that is corresponds to the
     size of your picture.
   - Modify the Nb of color of your page.

*"Grab Screen" Follow instructions.

*"Save", save the current picture.

*"Clear", erase the current picture (or several picture) and choose a
  background color.
   - Clears the gray pattern if you select Gray pattern by using
     the Diamond key. 
   - Clears the black pattern if you select Black pattern by using
     the Diamond key.

*"Show Page" display an idea of the current page (only if its size
  is bigger than the one of your Psion). Once "Show Page" is on,
  a cursor appears (it corresponds to the position of the current
  page's cursor), you can move this cursor and, when confirming
  with 'Space Bar' or 'Enter', both current page and cursor will be
  automaticaly set at the chosen position.

*"Print" sends current brush or current picture to the printer
  or into a file.
       Density Standard: max width of the picture: 480 pixels
               High : max width of the picture: 960 pixels
               High (Keep Ration) : max width of the picture :960 pixels
  Works well with Canon and Epson printers.
  (For registred users only)

*"About", Some useful information.


*"Quit", leaves PPaint.


IV/ Tools Menu:
----------------
All the tools functions use the setup that has been built
in the Styles menu.


     General use
     -----------
            - Use 'Space Bar' to draw a square or a circle, use it also
            to confirm most of the plain fonctions.
            - Use 'Enter' to draw a square or round surface with the
            texture chosen in the Styles menu.
            - 'Del' draw a square or a round surface, emptied, with
            a border without its grid.
            - 'Psion+Del' draws a square or a round surface without its
            grid.



*"Point" move Pen or Brush, use this function like Stamp, confirm the
position with 'Space' ---> to Add
           or 'Enter' ---> to Replace
           or 'Del'   ---> to Erase

*"Line", draws lines . Move the cursor using arrow keys,
  then press 'spacebar' to confirm each line's point.
          or 'Del' to clear line

*"Curve" draw a bezier curve.
 First, draw a line and  confirm it. A cursor will appear in the middle
 of the line. You can move this cursor with arrow keys, and a preview
 curve will be drawed.
 Confirm your curve with 'Space' key for an empty
 curve, or with 'Enter' key for a filled curve.

*"Polygon" draws continuous lines. Move the cursor using arrow keys
 then press 'Spacebar' to confirm each line's point.In order to draw
 the polygon with the selected pen:
       press 'Esc' for an empty polygon
          or 'Enter' to fill the polygon with the choosen pattern.
If you confirm your polygone with 'Diamond' key, your polygon
will be tranformed in Bspline.You can modify the step of the curve
in 'Custom/Parameters/Curve step'.

*"Box", draws a box. Move the cursor using arrow keys, press spacebar to
 confirm the first point of the box, then continue moving, the box will
 draw accordingly, press 'spacebar' or 'Enter' or 'DEl' or 'Psion+Del'
 to confirm.
 
*"Ellipse", draws ellipses. Move the cursor using arrow keys, press
 'Spacebar'. An axe will appear, showing you the diameter. You can alter
 it using arrow keys,press 'spacebar' or 'Enter' or 'DEl' or 'Psion+Del'
 to confirm.

*"Spray", move the cursor using arrow keys, press 'Spacebar' or 'Del' to
 confirm.
 The spay can be modified using SPRAY LX, SPRAY LY, SPRAY Tp.
 The spray conform to the selected texture.

*"FILL", fills a closed surface with the selected texture.
 Move the cursor then confirm the fill command with 'Space'
 An error like 'Invalid arg' meens that your surface is not
 closed.


V/ Styles Menu:
-------------
*"Fill Pattern", allows you to choose a different filling mode.

     SPARE : allows you to fill your shade with datas coming from the
     spare page (if this one is active).

     Brush : allows you to fill your shade with the curent brush, wich
     will act as a pattern. It will be drawn regulary from right to left,
     by raws and columns until the complete shade is filled.

     Brush-Wall: This mode filling is pretty much like  the mode "Brush",
     but each row is displaced a half-width of brush as compared to the
     precedent as in a wall bricks.
     
     Brush-mirror: this one is made of a succession of reflections (left,
     right, top, bottom) of the current brush.

     Inverted : Inverts the current texture.

     Standard : restores plain black for filling.

*"Pen" changes the pen's aspect.
  - normal : classical pen : the point.
  - Brush : Uses current brush for drawing.
  - Custom : allows you to chose a different pen than the point.
  - Anim : lets you chose an animated pen.

     - Every Nth dot : Allows you not to have a regular drawing.
     - Show Brush : allows you to see the brush either as a
       pre-visualization or fully as it has been captured.
     -"AnimPainting" allows you to draw object and animate in the
       same time.Usefull for cycling animation.
       First you have to create an animation and
       you have to select a pen different than the point.

*"Mode" Selects the drawing mode
  "Set"
  "Clear"
  "Negative"
  "Replace"

*"Text", allows to write on the page, using the style and font
 (internal or external).

  Text : allows you to write.(you can specify the orientation
  of the text: Vertical or horizontal).
  ASCII : allows you to add in text an ASCII character.
  Insert ASCII :Insert ascii text at the current position of the cursor.
  STYLE : select the style.
  FONT : you can choose between internal or external font.
  SHOW ASCII : show the ASCII table of the current font.

The text will appear on the page, use it like a brush.



VI/ Custom menu :
-----------------
*"Startup Prefs" lets you chose
  - screen size,
  - Use grey(Yes/No)
    If you chose not to use grey color, you spare memory and all
    functions will be more faster.
  - Undo (Yes/No)
  - Spare (Yes/No) 
    if undo and Spare page are not activated, you gain memory.
  - Textures (Yes/No) (If you choose 'No', you spare memory, You can
    load very big picture but 'Fill pattern' and 'Textures editor'
    are no longer available.
  - "Restore Icon" If you don't keep this option you can save memory.
  - the language (French, English)

*"Open Prefs" Loads the first preferences.

*"Info" indicates the size of the page and the one of the Brush
 (If it exists)

*"General Prefs" Lets you chose 
    - the speed at which your cursor moves or
    - keep pattern ...

*"Tools Prefs"
    - Ellipse: steps of the Ellipse function.
    - Bspline: step of the curve (0.01,0.1)
       0.01 meens 100 (1/0.01) lines in the curve
       0.1 meens 10 (1/0.1) lines in the curve
       More the number of line is important, more the curve is precise, 
       but more the drawing or filling is slow
    - Fill
    - Spray: LX: Width of the spray
             LY: Height of the Spray
             Tp: Number of Particle.


*"Spare" The current page is set in the background and the spared page
 appears, you can work on it naturally like you would have done on the
 current page . If you select it again the spared page will come back
 to the background and the current page will appear again.

*"Undo" to cancel the last operation done on the picture, if you select
 it again you anihilate the cancelation.

*"Coords ON" / "Coords OFF" : displays or not the cursor's XY coordinates.



VII/ Brush menu :
-----------------
*"Load" loads a picture as a brush. Move it with arrow keys, print it to
 page with spacebar (it is added to screen content) or enter (replace the
 screen portion with the brush) or ESC empties screen with brush.

*"Save" Saves the current brush.

*"Free" destroys current brush (to spare memory)

*"Pick up" allows you to pick up a portion of screen to use it as a brush.
 Draw the selection box as you would for a standard box using the spacebar
 key, the cutted picture will be displayed next to the box. Once this is
 done, you can alter or move it, then draw it on screen.
 If you Confirm your selection with 'Del' instead of 'Space', you pick up
 the brush and delete it from your current page.

*"Pick Icon" used to save an icon and choose its borders.

*"Restore" restores the brush's original state (If you chose this option)

*"Distort" alter a brush
     "Flip" flips it on X or Y axis.
     "Shear" Shears the brush on X or Y axis.
     "Bend" Bends the brush
     "Rotate" Rotates the brush 90ø, 45ø or at any angle
     "Size" changes the brush size.
     "Negative" invert brush's colors.


VIII/ Effects Menu :
--------------------
 Select a part of the screen before apply an effect.
 If you have created an animation,you can specify on what frames
 the effect can be applied.

*"Select Zone" select the part of the screen you would like to apply
 the effect by drawing a rectangle.

*"Select from center" select the part of the screen you would like to apply
 the effect by drawing a rectangle centered by cursor.

*"Select All" Select whole picture.

*"Show zone"

*"Apply Effect"

   "Outline" Outlines drawing.

   "Wrap" Quickly changes all the sufaces textures.

   "Noise" Adds noise on picture. You can select horizontal or vertical noise,
    or both. You can also change noise amplitude.

   "Relief"

 For registred users only:

   "Pattern" allows you to copy, move, exchange patterns between them.

   "Gradient" allows you to make dithtering between White, gray & Black.

   "Mosaic" allows you to pixelize your image,effectively reducing its
    resolution.You can select pixels size, Offset (to reproduce wall) or
    Background color.

   "Wave" or Ripple allows you to make wave distortion, just enter
    the amplitude.

   "Loupe effect" allows you to map any image onto a sphere.
     
   "Explode"This effect subdivides the image into a grid
    of user-specified mosaic tiles.




IX/ Modules  menu :
--------------------
*"Textures Editor" allows you to build, modify and choose you filling
 texture. First, a requester ask for a panel in the current directory.
 The panel is then displayed, you can move in using arrow keys.
 If you press 'Enter', you select a texture and quit the editor.
 If you press 'Esc', you quit the editor without texture.

  TEXTURE SET
  "Load panel" loads a new panel.
  "Save panel" save the current panel with modifications.
  "Save panel as" saves the current panel with a new name
  "Restore panel" restores the original panel
  "New" Displays a new panel
  "Select & quit" Select the texture and go back to main picture.
  "Quit" Quits without modification.

  EDIT TEXTURE
  "Edit" Edits the current texture, Enter to confirm changes, diamond 
     to change color, Esc aborts.
                       "Flip/x"
                       "Flip/y"
                       "Rotate 90ø"
                       "Negative"
                       "Clear"
     "Copy" Copies the texture in memory.
     "Paste" pastes the memorised texture at cursor.
     "Brush -> Text" Transforms the current brush into texture.
     "Text -> Brush" Transforms the current texture into brush.

  WARNING 
  -------
  If you create a new panel of textures or modify an existing
  panel and that you quit the editor without having saved your work...
  It will be lost.

*"Zoom" allows you to zoom a part of the current picture, you can so work
 point by point.
 'Arrows key' or 'Psion+Arrows key' to move, spacebar to toggle point, 
 diamond key to select color.
     "Zoom in" to raise zoom level.
     "Zoom out" to lower zoom level.
     "Center"centres the drawing according to the cursor.
     "Preference" sets the editing size of the zoom.
     "Quit" to go back to drawing, changes are saved.

*"Copy to ..." allows you to copy:
               - Current Page to Spare Page
          or   - Current Page to Brush
          or   - Spare Page to Current Page
          or   - Spare Page to Brush
          or   - Brush to Current Page

   Very handy to use brush distorsions on current picture or page's effects on brush

   Samples:

      --> Use brush distortions on current picture:
              - Copy current page to brush  
                (Picture/Copy to .../Current page to brush)
              - Make a distorsion
                (Brush/Distort)
              - Copy brush to current page
                (Picture/Copy to .../Brush to current page)
 
     --> Use page's effects on brush:
              - Copy Brush to current page
                (Picture/Copy to .../brush to current page)
              - Apply an effects
                (Modules/Effects)
              - Copy current page to brush
                (Picture/Copy to .../Current page to Brush)

     --> Reduce page's size without erasing it:
              - Pick up the part of the page you want to keep
                (Brush/Pick up)
              - Copy brush to current page
                (Picture/Copy to .../Brush to Current page)

     --> Increase page's size without erasing it:
              - Copy current page to brush
                (Picture/Copy to .../Current page to brush)
              - Change page's size
                (Custom/Preferences)
              - Place the brush wherever you want.



X/ Anim Menu:
--------------
(For registred users only)

* "Load" loads several images so as to construct an animation.
  All frames must have the same format.

 In the requester you have to enter the first frame and the last.
 Ppaint will load all images between the two selections,
 and this by alphabetical order.

* "Save"saves the animation in a series of frame in PIC format (or in PCX
   , GIF if you install the externals libraries).

* "Free" erases the animation and liberates memory.

* "Create" allows you to create an animation, enter just the number of frame.

* "Edit" allows to manipulate the animation
           - "Delete" Delete current frame or several frames.
           - "Copy" copies current frame on all the animation
              or on specify frame.
              you can also copy a whole sequence.
           - "Insert"  allows you to insert a certain number of frame has left
              the current frame. The current frame will be automatically
              copied on frames inserted.

* "AutoAnim"  You specify characteristic of the first Frame and
  the last (position of the brush, rotation, scale)
  and Ppaint tends to construct the animation
  with fade in or fade out effect.
  For this function, you ,first, have to create an anim and
  pick up a brush.

* "Go to" allows you to go directly to a frame. You have just to
  specify the number of the frame.

* "Play" you can play the animation forward, backward or in Ping-Pong.
  You can also specify the speed of the animation. If you enter a pause
  has 0, the animation will play frame by frame.




XI/ HISTORY :
------------

V1.0
First version for Psion series 3

V2.0
First version for Psion series 3A

V2.3   
- many bugs have been rectified, notably on the loading of fonts,
  textures, Pictures,management of errors...
- Optimisation of the memory with dynamic page management.
- Graphic elevator integrated in functions of distortion
- Function Restores
- Possibility to use as brush brush it
- New brushes
- New panels of texture
- The mode brushes is no longer blocked to its displacement and to its
  display, but all the other functions are accessible.
- Function Reset

V2.4
- Ppaint is bilingual (French/English)

V2.5
- Icon capture with borders
- Window gestion rebuilt
- Quit ascii table, entirely restores the picture
- Chinese effect erase from the program

V2.6
- More brush deformation
- New texture: mirror Brush
- rewritten effects
- restore Icon becomes an option
- New Brush transformation
- The drawing of the Ellipse changes with the step chosen
- 'TAB' key toggle between plain pen and brush
- New features in zoom editor
- Size of the icon available
- State Window
- Anim pen

V2.7
- Little bug on the text function (Corrected)
- Size of the page limited by the memory
- Choice of a background color
- Prefs can be saved

V2.8
- More stable version
- Many small bugs have been corrected
   (Correction of errors, relief Effect, Warp Effect ,
  All tools,  keyboard, text function, display...)
- Help on-line in English and French
- Shift + Arrows Keys move cursor one pixel per one pixel
- Tool 'Fill'  entirely rewritten,it fills, now, all surfaces
  completely.
- You can automatically draw in gray over black pattern with
  all tools. (originally on the Psion when you  use gray pattern,
  this last is found always in rear plan by report of black pattern,
  and therefore is hidden)
- For recorded users, new two effects:
    - Effect 'Pattern' allows you to copy, move or exchange
      patterns between them.
    - Effect 'Gradient' allow you to make gradations, with an
      orderly dithtering, between the three colors
      (White, Gray and Black), vertical or horizontal manner.

V2.9
- New parameter available when initializing
  the screen:Texture (Yes/No). If you select No,
  you spare memory. Then you load and work on much
  bigger pictures, on the other hand, some functions
  of Ppaint won't be available any more.
  (Styles/Fill pattern and Modules/Textures editor)
- Dynamic initialization of the screen: after each
  initialization, Ppaint displays an information concerning
  what he could confirm, according memory available
  (screen's size, number of colors ...).
- New item: Brush/Free: Kills the current brush and
  therefore frees memory.
- The brush is no longer automatically destroyed after each
  initialisation of the screen.
- Rotation optimized,more faster,better aspect.
- All the effects available have been gathered in
  the 'Modules' menu under the name of 'Effects'.
- New effect: Mosaique (only for registred users)
- New function: 'Copy to ...'
  Very handy to use brush distorsions on current picture or
  page's effects on brush (see doc and samples)
- Several icons in the state window have been redrawn.
- Small bug corrected on ellipses, better aspect.
- The tool 'Line' doesn't allow you to draw continuous lines
  any more, for this function use the new tool 'Polygon' which
  also enables you to fill automatically all drawn polygons
  with the choosen texture.
- New function: 'Show page' gives an idea of the current page
  (when its size is bigger than the Psion's screen) in order
  to visualize it totally.
- Translation (French-English) improved.
- menus reorganised
- Some names have been changed
- And of course...some bugs corrected.

V2.91
- When you load a picture, Ppaint detects automatically the
  nb of color of your picture.
- New function: Print, with many options
  (For registred users only)
- New function: Insert ASCII, insert ascii text at the current
  position of the cursor.
- Doc and help on-line are updated.
- You can choose Spare page for background in Mosaic effect.
- 3 new brush anim (Chalk aspect) (Nø9,10,11)
- And some bugs corrected.

V3.0:
- You can Load, save and edit animation
  so there is a new Menu 'ANIM' and new Items (Read the Doc).
- New option in 'Styles/Pen', 'AnimPainting'. It allows you to draw object
  and animate in the same time.Usefull for cycling animation.
  First you have to create an animation and
  you have to select a pen different than the point.
- 'Clear' function has been improved, you can now clear several pictures in
  the same time. (For animation)
- You can Import & Export GIF and PCX format with externals libraries
  (Read the Doc)
- Improved Circles aspect.
- Now when you draw an object, Ppaint shows you the size of your object.
- Some bugs corrected (Zoom, Textures editor ...).

V 3.1
- text ,now, can be oriented vertically.
- 3 new effects: Wave(or ripple), loupe effects and explode.
- New tools: Curve.
- if you confirm your polygone with 'Diamond' key,
  your polygone will be transformed in Bspline.
- New function: AutoAnim:
  You specify characteristic of the first Frame and
  the last (position of the brush, rotation, scale)
  and Ppaint tends to construct the animation
  with fade in or fade out effect.
- Effects can now be applied on all an animation automatically.

V3.2
- for each procedure, Ppaint eats uselessly some memory, now
 the bug is corrected.
- New label: Grab Screen
- Rewritten Textures Editor
- When you pick up a brush, if you confirme with 'Del' instead of 'Space', you pick up
 the brush and delete it from your current page.
- New menu: Effects
  Now you have to select a zone before apply an effect.
  You can select a zone or the entire picture.
- New icon system
- New panel of texture and clipArt.
- All tools prefs have been gathered in
  the 'Custom' menu under the name of 'Tools Prefs'.
- Bug corrected with old Keys.


XII/ Advise :
------------
- If a function doesn't react properly, check if the pattern has been
  correctly chosen.
- If because of a lack of memory or a mistake in the use of a function,
  you cannot use Ppaint, come back to the system screen, go to the Ppaint
  program and quit it with 'Del'.
- Most of the problems you may have with Ppaint come from a lake of memory.
  You must bear in mind that even with a 2Mo Psion, a task started by the
  Psion cannot use all the memory available, because the Psion still thinks
  it can use only (512 Ko).

